{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25600188",
      "title": "How To Work With Redux State Correctly",
      "sourceHash": "8a831230f9da98ee8a8379a663223d180c26f8f8456d6825571b65e26c108f49",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.19,
          "end": 4.43,
          "en": "Now let's talk about the objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.43,
          "end": 9.34,
          "en": "which we are returning in our reducer, in our Redux reducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.34,
          "end": 12.74,
          "en": "I mentioned in the last lecture that we always",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.74,
          "end": 17.54,
          "en": "return a brand new snapshot, a brand new state object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.54,
          "end": 22.02,
          "en": "which Redux will use to replace its existing state with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 22.02,
          "end": 24,
          "en": "So the objects which we return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 24,
          "end": 28.47,
          "en": "in the reducer will not, and that's super important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 28.47,
          "end": 31.97,
          "en": "will not be merged with the existing state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 31.97,
          "end": 35.42,
          "en": "They will overwrite the existing state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 35.42,
          "end": 38.86,
          "en": "So if we, for example going set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 38.86,
          "end": 41.45,
          "en": "show counter here when we incremented",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.45,
          "end": 45.62,
          "en": "because before it got to add it here, if we do this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 45.62,
          "end": 49.413,
          "en": "if I click increment, you see I close my counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 50.44,
          "end": 52.88,
          "en": "I closed my counter when I click increment even",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 52.88,
          "end": 56.96,
          "en": "though I shouldn't, because I don't set show counter here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 56.96,
          "end": 59.9,
          "en": "hence it's basically removed from the object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 59.9,
          "end": 62.78,
          "en": "and it has a value of undefined therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 62.78,
          "end": 65.66,
          "en": "an undefined is treated as false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.66,
          "end": 68.12,
          "en": "So we don't render to counter then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 68.12,
          "end": 70.145,
          "en": "And that's of course a side-effect, which we don't want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.145,
          "end": 71.623,
          "en": "That's an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.53,
          "end": 76.9,
          "en": "So we must always set all the other states",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.9,
          "end": 79.11,
          "en": "when we update a piece of state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 80,
          "end": 82.513,
          "en": "because we overwrite the old state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.71000000000001,
          "end": 85.67,
          "en": "Now that brings up one question.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 85.67,
          "end": 89.33,
          "en": "Why do we need to return a new piece of data here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.33,
          "end": 91.95,
          "en": "Why can't we just use the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.95,
          "end": 95.6,
          "en": "which we're getting as an argument, access counter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 95.6,
          "end": 98.763,
          "en": "and increment it like this, instead of returning?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.65,
          "end": 103.61,
          "en": "Or maybe we do it like this, and then we return state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 103.61,
          "end": 106.74000000000001,
          "en": "And when we do that, we changed state before we return it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.74000000000001,
          "end": 108.693,
          "en": "And then we just return it again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 109.53,
          "end": 114.53,
          "en": "Well, if we do that and we reload, everything works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 115.49000000000001,
          "end": 118.06,
          "en": "So it's not easy to see that this is wrong,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 118.06,
          "end": 120.82,
          "en": "but it is, even though it works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 120.82,
          "end": 125.18,
          "en": "This is something you absolutely must not do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 125.18,
          "end": 127.21,
          "en": "when working with Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 127.21,
          "end": 130.8,
          "en": "You should never super important never",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 130.8,
          "end": 133.6,
          "en": "mutate the state, the existing state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 133.6,
          "end": 136.67000000000002,
          "en": "You should never change the existing state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 136.67000000000002,
          "end": 139.56,
          "en": "Instead, always override it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 139.56,
          "end": 143.2,
          "en": "by returning a brand new state object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.2,
          "end": 147.24,
          "en": "And because objects and arrays are reference values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 147.24,
          "end": 151.27,
          "en": "in JavaScript, it's easy to accidentally override",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 151.27,
          "end": 153.55,
          "en": "and change the existing state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.55,
          "end": 155.57999999999998,
          "en": "You could for example think that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 155.57999999999998,
          "end": 157.51,
          "en": "you can do something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 157.51,
          "end": 160.59,
          "en": "And then you return a new object where you then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 160.59,
          "end": 164.29,
          "en": "do set to counter to state.counter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 164.29,
          "end": 167.573,
          "en": "and show counter to state.showcounter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 168.87,
          "end": 171.72,
          "en": "We can do this because we changed the counter here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 171.72,
          "end": 173.88,
          "en": "And then we returned a brand new object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 173.88,
          "end": 175.78,
          "en": "Everything's good, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 175.78,
          "end": 177.54,
          "en": "Well, again, that will work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177.54,
          "end": 181.21,
          "en": "If I reload, it works, but it's still super bad",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 181.21,
          "end": 186,
          "en": "because we still mutate the existing state because objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 186,
          "end": 189.99,
          "en": "and arrays are reference values in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 189.99,
          "end": 193.22,
          "en": "And in case it's not clear to you What I mean by that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 193.22,
          "end": 196.01,
          "en": "Attached you find a link which leads you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 196.01,
          "end": 200.03300000000002,
          "en": "to an article and a video where I explained this in depth.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 200.9,
          "end": 203.41,
          "en": "Now, when working with redux and it's state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 203.41,
          "end": 206.28,
          "en": "you must never mutate state like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 206.28,
          "end": 209.76,
          "en": "never changed the original state which you're getting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 209.76,
          "end": 213.4,
          "en": "This can lead to bugs, unpredictable behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 213.4,
          "end": 217.5,
          "en": "and it can make debugging your application harder as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 217.5,
          "end": 220.13,
          "en": "So even though it doesn't lead to a bug here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 220.13,
          "end": 223.47,
          "en": "it can have unwanted and unexpected side effects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 223.47,
          "end": 227.68,
          "en": "in bigger applications where your state gets out of sync.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 227.68,
          "end": 231.46,
          "en": "And suddenly the UI is not reflecting your state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 231.46,
          "end": 232.72,
          "en": "correctly anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 232.72,
          "end": 235.38,
          "en": "And hence the simple rule is never",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 235.38,
          "end": 237.06,
          "en": "mutate your state like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 237.06,
          "end": 239.63,
          "en": "Always return a brand new object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 239.63,
          "end": 243.06,
          "en": "where you copy any nested objects or erase.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 243.06,
          "end": 246.87,
          "en": "If you have any and create brand new values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 246.87,
          "end": 248.51,
          "en": "as we're doing it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 248.51,
          "end": 250.68,
          "en": "By updating our state like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 250.68,
          "end": 255.1,
          "en": "we create a brand new object where we don't change anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 255.1,
          "end": 257.52,
          "en": "And especially when you have a state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 257.52,
          "end": 259.75,
          "en": "with nested objects and arrays",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 259.75,
          "end": 262.89,
          "en": "it's easy to accidentally mutate your existing state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 262.89,
          "end": 265.12,
          "en": "And therefore you should be super careful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 265.12,
          "end": 267.55,
          "en": "that you do this in an immutable way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 267.55,
          "end": 271.2,
          "en": "that you'd never accidentally mutate your existing state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 271.2,
          "end": 274.3,
          "en": "but you copy any objects which you added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 274.3,
          "end": 277.953,
          "en": "So you always create a brand new object or array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 277.953,
          "end": 280.64,
          "en": "Whenever you need to update data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 280.64,
          "end": 283.65999999999997,
          "en": "you never just dive into an existing object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 283.65999999999997,
          "end": 286.64,
          "en": "and start manipulating its properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 286.64,
          "end": 290.48,
          "en": "Always copy and create new objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 290.48,
          "end": 293.11,
          "en": "Now, at this point it might look a little bit too early",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 293.11,
          "end": 294.76,
          "en": "to emphasize it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 294.76,
          "end": 297.33,
          "en": "because this is a fairly simple state here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 297.33,
          "end": 299.96,
          "en": "but it is super important, easy to mess up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 299.96,
          "end": 302.83,
          "en": "and something you should know right from the start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 302.83,
          "end": 305.343,
          "en": "which is why I am emphasizing it here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}